+    round-6 breadth campaign, results/outer_loop_fable5_ka59_probe.json):
+    fixed round 5''s tooling bug (a two-layer-safe frame printer) and got
+    real L7 exploration this time -- 203 live calls. Confirmed the
+    helper-to-helper ballistics from round 4 generalize but are
+    DIRECTIONAL and ORDER-SENSITIVE: a selected horizontal 6x3 helper
+    aligned immediately above the vertical 3x6 helper launches the
+    vertical helper 15 pixels downward through the otherwise solid lower
+    partition. The INVERSE arrangement (selected vertical helper pushing
+    the horizontal helper sideways) stayed blocked across every tested
+    exact/partial alignment, approach momentum, and all six cycling-stack
+    phases -- a real asymmetry, not an unexplored gap. Also found the
+    rectangular helpers canNOT relocate the lower cycling stack from
+    either side, unlike L6''s selected square (a capability the square
+    piece had that these rectangles lack). Direct ACTION6 probes on the
+    plus, cycling stack, color-15 partitions, and color-2 barriers were
+    all inert. No fresh reproduction gate run (the 358-call prefix alone
+    exceeded the remaining budget). No new level banked; frontier stays
+    at level 6.'
